# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the working tree
# while dprint (which has no newlineKind set in dprint.json, so it defaults to LF) expects LF. The
# result was that `bun run fmt:check` reported every one of its ~123 covered files as
# "Text differed by line endings" on every run, so the pre-commit hook could never pass and the
# formatting/lint gate it exists to enforce was effectively dead.
#
# `text=auto` lets git normalize to LF in the repository and auto-detect binary content;
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf so the working tree also gets LF, which is what dprint reads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, regardless of the auto-detection above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.wasm binary
